    {
      "id": "f332be45-4b18-4459-887d-6b470d07839e",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2448,
        -2144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 2016,
        "height": 1280,
        "content": "# Part 1 \u2014 AI Facebook Comment Auto-Reply\n\nAn advanced, production-ready n8n system that automates Facebook Page comment replies using an **AI Agent** (OpenRouter):\n\n1. **Webhook & Verification:** Receives real-time Meta webhook events and handles verification challenges (`hub.challenge`).\n2. **Security Filtering:** Filters valid comments and automatically ignores page self-comments to prevent infinite automated loops.\n3. **Context Enrichment:** Fetches the original Facebook Post content via Graph API to provide full conversational context.\n4. **AI Processing & Tools:**\n   - Powered by OpenRouter LLM.\n   - **Postgres Chat Memory:** Keeps track of isolated, ongoing conversations per user on a per-post basis (`Post ID + User ID`).\n   - **Supabase Vector Store (RAG):** Automatically queries internal knowledge base documents as a tool to ensure precise, fact-based answers.\n5. **Auto-Response:** Directly publishes the AI-generated response as a threaded reply to the specific customer comment via Facebook Graph API."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ad102d47-b624-406b-8f47-99ff4297e2a7",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1232,
        -2144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1168,
        "height": 2176,
        "content": "# ENTERPRISE RAG ECOSYSTEM: AI FACEBOOK COMMENT AUTO-REPLY & DRIVE KNOWLEDGE SYNC\n\n## Executive Summary & Architecture Overview\nThis production-grade n8n automation ecosystem bridges the gap between static enterprise documentation (Google Drive) and real-time social media customer engagement (Facebook Pages). \nBy combining a self-updating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline with an intelligent AI Agent, Postgres Persistent Memory, and Supabase Vector Store, this system ensures your Facebook Fanpage responds to customer comments instantly, accurately, and with precise context.\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites & Credentials Setup\n\nBefore running or publishing this workflow, ensure you have configured the following credentials in your n8n instance:\n\n1. **OpenRouter API Account:** Required to power the AI Agent LLM model.\n2. **OpenAI API Account:** Required for generating document embeddings (`Embeddings OpenAI` / `Embed the query`).\n3. **Supabase Account & Vector Store Setup:** \n   - Create a Supabase project and enable `pgvector`.\n   - You need to create the vector table named `documents`. Follow the official guide here: [Supabase LangChain AI Integration Guide](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/ai/langchain?database-method=sql).\n4. **PostgreSQL Database Account:** \n   - Required for `Postgres Chat Memory` to isolate conversation history per user per post.\n5. **Google Drive OAuth2 API:** \n   - Required to monitor the watched folders (`Google Drive Trigger` & file operations).\n6. **Facebook Graph API Account:** \n   - Requires a Page Access Token with permissions: `pages_manage_posts`, `pages_read_engagement`, and `pages_messaging` (or comment management permissions).\n\n---\n\n## Facebook Webhook & n8n Webhook Configuration Guide\n\nTo receive real-time comments from your Facebook Page, you must set up a Meta App and configure the n8n Webhook node:\n\n1. **Configure n8n Webhook:** \n   - Refer to the official [n8n Webhook Node Documentation](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.webhook) for detailed configuration options (such as handling challenge verification methods and routing).\n2. **Configure Meta for Developers:**\n   - Go to Meta for Developers and create/select your app.\n   - Add the **Webhooks** product and select **Page** subscription.\n   - **Callback URL:** Paste your n8n Webhook production URL.\n   - **Verify Token:** Enter the secret token matching your configuration.\n   - Subscribe to the `feed` (or `comments`) field.\n3. Once verified, the webhook will automatically handle Meta's initial verification challenge (`hub.challenge`) and process incoming comment events.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Breakdown of the 4 System Parts\n\n### Part 1: AI Facebook Comment Auto-Reply Engine\n- **Objective:** Automatically handle inbound comment traffic on Facebook posts with human-like, accurate, and polite responses.\n- **Key Components & Flow:**\n  1. **Webhook & Challenge Verification:** Intercepts real-time Meta webhook payloads and handles verification challenges (`hub.challenge`) smoothly.\n  2. **Security & Loop Filters:** Evaluates whether the incoming payload is a valid comment and strictly filters out page self-comments to prevent infinite automated reply loops.\n  3. **Context Enrichment:** Automatically queries the Facebook Graph API to retrieve the original post content, giving the LLM full background on what the customer is talking about.\n  4. **AI Agent & OpenRouter LLM:** The core processing brain using advanced language models to generate natural, conversational replies.\n  5. **Postgres Chat Memory:** Maintains isolated, thread-safe conversation histories per user on a per-post basis using a composite session key (`Post ID + User ID`). This allows the bot to remember previous turns in a comment thread with a specific user.\n  6. **Supabase Vector Store (RAG Tool):** Acts as the retrieval tool, querying the synchronized knowledge base to pull factual product info, pricing, or policies before writing a response.\n  7. **Auto-Response Execution:** Publishes the final AI-generated response directly as a threaded reply to the user's specific comment ID via the Facebook Graph API.\n\n### Part 2: Automated File Ingestion Pipeline (New Files)\n- **Objective:** Keep the AI knowledge base perpetually updated without manual intervention.\n- **Flow:**\n  1. **Google Drive Trigger:** Continuously monitors a dedicated folder for newly created PDF documents.\n  2. **Extraction & Processing:** Downloads the binary file, converts/reads it, and extracts clean raw text.\n  3. **Chunking & Embedding:** Splits the text into optimal semantic chunks and generates vector embeddings using OpenAI models.\n  4. **Vector Indexing:** Upserts the embedded chunks directly into the Supabase `documents` table, making them instantly available for the AI Agent in Part 1.\n\n### Part 3: Knowledge Base Version Control (Updated Files)\n- **Objective:** Ensure no outdated information remains in the AI's memory when source documents change.\n- **Flow:**\n  1. **Drive Update Trigger:** Detects modifications or new versions of existing files in the watched folder.\n  2. **Vector Purging:** Automatically scans Supabase and deletes all outdated vector chunks associated with that specific file (matched via metadata `fileName`).\n  3. **Re-Indexing:** Seamlessly downloads the updated file, extracts fresh text, re-chunks, re-embeds, and re-indexes the new content into Supabase.\n\n### Part 4: Automated Cleanup & Sync (Deleted Files)\n- **Objective:** Prevent hallucinations or incorrect answers derived from deleted or deprecated business documents.\n- **Flow:**\n  1. **Trash / Deletion Trigger:** Fires when a file is deleted or moved to the trash folder on Google Drive.\n  2. **Database Scrubbing:** Instantly removes all corresponding vector embeddings from the Supabase knowledge base.\n  3. **Clean Sync:** Keeps the vector store lean, secure, and 100% synchronized with your active Google Drive workspace."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
